course: dictionary
lesson: 9349
title: Splat and sound words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like what they mean. Say splat out loud: splat! It is an onomatopoeia, like bang, pop and splash. Context helps you learn it. «Springy things store a push: a stretched rubber band or a trampoline springs back and gives the push back, while a lump of clay just goes splat.»
explain: The clue is the difference between the two things. The rubber band and trampoline spring back, but the clay does not bounce. It just goes splat, so splat must mean squashing flat with a wet, slapping sound. Try your meaning in the sentence: «a lump of clay just squashes flat with a wet sound» still makes sense.
explain: Splat can be a noun, a verb or an interjection. A splat is a messy mark. To splat is to hit something with this sound, or to squash it flat. Splat! on its own is the sound itself. Each one is still the same wet, slapping idea.
fact: Splat is the wet slapping sound something soft makes when it hits a surface hard.
fact: Splat is an onomatopoeia: a word that sounds like what it means.
fact: A splat is a messy mark made when something soft hits a surface.
fact: To splat means to hit something with this sound, or to squash it flat.
fact: Other onomatopoeia words include bang, pop and splash.
exercise: «Springy things store a push, while a lump of clay just goes splat.» What does splat mean in this sentence? | Shines brightly | Whispers quietly | *Squashes flat with a wet sound | Bounces back strongly
exercise: Which word is an onomatopoeia, a word that sounds like what it means? | *Pop | Gentle | Happy | Slowly
exercise: Tom finds a splat of tomato on the kitchen wall. What is a splat here? | A kind of trampoline | A sleepy yawn | *A messy mark made by something soft hitting a surface | A long, thin piece of string
test: «That white splat on the car is not poo at all but the bird's version of wee.» What is the splat in this sentence? | A shiny, clean wipe | A small, dry leaf | *A messy mark left when something soft hits a surface | A loud musical note
test: Which word means to hit something with a wet slapping sound? | *To splat | To sparkle | To yawn | To hum
exam: Which of these is the sound a soft thing makes when it hits a hard surface? | Drift | Sunny | Hush | *Splat!
